# The line coverage the tests must not fall below, in percent, as
# tests/coverage.py measures it over both toolkits merged. The coverage job in
# .github/workflows/ui.yml fails when the number is under it; see AGENTS.md §3.
#
# It sits about 0.3 pp under what the tests actually reach, because a UI run is
# not deterministic to the hundredth: medit is started again when it could not
# open the display, timers and idle handlers fire or do not, and the tests run
# in parallel.
#
# Raise it when a full point has opened up above it, to the new number less the
# same margin, in the commit that earns the rise -- the job says so and prints
# the line to write. A tenth would be chasing jitter; a point is the most this
# file ever leaves undefended. Lowering it is a legitimate commit too, when
# covered code was deleted or a test was retired, with the reason written here
# beside the number.
#
# 2026-09-07  41.57% measured on the first run: 32 UI tests and 17 unit tests,
#             gtk2 at 38.56% and gtk3 at 41.37%.
# 2026-09-08  42.97%, raised to 42.7: five more of the language server protocol
#             answered, with five UI tests and twenty unit tests behind them --
#             gtk2 at 39.71%, gtk3 at 42.80%, and src/plugins/lsp at 85.41%.
# 2026-09-08  43.84%, raised to 43.5: the shortcuts dialog is driven now, and
#             the accelerator map with it -- two UI tests, and a third that
#             rebinds the terminal's keys before pressing them.
43.5
